# .env — read by the runner itself and applied to every job it accepts.
#
# What this file turns on, stated accurately — an earlier version of this comment claimed
# universal containerisation, and a smoke job declaring no container proved otherwise by
# reporting ISOLATION=host.
#
# The container hooks manage containers for a job that DECLARES one (`container:` /
# `services:`), giving it a consistent runtime and cleanup. They do NOT place an
# undeclared job into a container: such a job executes against this host's filesystem as
# the unprivileged runner account. Per-job containerisation is therefore NOT an enforced
# isolation control here; what is enforced is the workspace wipe below, the unprivileged
# account, and the host's egress denial.
#
# The hooks shell out to a `docker` binary, found on the runner's PATH: /usr/bin/docker,
# Docker's CLI client (docker-ce-cli, installed by install-podman.yml with
# podman_docker_api_client). It is only a client: every call goes to the API socket below,
# served by this account's rootless podman (its podman.socket user unit). There is no
# Docker engine on this host.
ACTIONS_RUNNER_CONTAINER_HOOKS={{ github_runner_home }}/_hooks/index.js

# The engine the hooks' docker talks to: this account's rootless podman API socket.
# The hooks start `docker` with only the job's variables (HOME=/github/home among them)
# plus the DOCKER_* variables of the runner, which they pass through on purpose
# (runner-container-hooks v0.8.1, utils.ts optionsWithDockerEnvs). So this value reaches
# every hook call, while the job's HOME never reaches podman: the API service runs with
# the account's own environment. Run as a CLI with the job's HOME, podman failed every
# container job with `cannot resolve /github/home` (docs/MISTAKES.md 10.25, 10.28).
# Every host step inherits this too, so a plain step's `docker` uses the same engine and
# image store as the hooks. The runner reads this file only when it starts, so the
# deploy restarts it on a change.
DOCKER_HOST=unix:///run/user/{{ github_runner_uid }}/podman/podman.sock

# Runs before EVERY job. Creates the directories the runner bind-mounts into a job
# container: podman, unlike Docker, refuses a bind mount whose source is missing.
# The runner reads this file only when it starts, so the deploy restarts it on a change.
ACTIONS_RUNNER_HOOK_JOB_STARTED={{ github_runner_home }}/job-started.sh

# Runs after EVERY job — success, failure, or cancellation — and destroys the job's
# workspace and containers. Second layer on purpose: the container boundary above is a
# single mechanism protecting several repositories from each other, and a workspace wipe
# is cheap enough to be worth having behind it.
ACTIONS_RUNNER_HOOK_JOB_COMPLETED={{ github_runner_home }}/job-cleanup.sh
